IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- THE FOURTH SCHEDULE (COURT FEES): THE TYPES AND THE ARITHMETIC (part roc12, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- The Schedule is data: each row of each table is a constant of type `sch 4 row` in the file for its Part, and each
-- fee in a cell is a `sch 4 fee`.  This file holds the types and the functions that turn a fee into a number.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  `MAYBE NUMBER` answers carry JUST number when the Schedule states the sum, and NOTHING when it
-- states the fee in words only (for example "such fee ... as appears to the Registrar to be fair and reasonable").
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into 0.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Fourth Schedule -- the columns, the fees and the rows`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The columns the tables name.  "Supreme Court" has two (the value of the claim up to or over $1 million);
-- "State Courts" has the District Court and the Magistrate's Court.  Table 4 of Part 2 has one General Division column.
DECLARE `sch 4 column` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million`
    `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million`
    `sch 4 column District Court`
    `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court`
    `sch 4 column General Division`

-- One fee as a cell states it.  The words of a cell that none of the shapes fits are kept as `a fee stated in words`.
DECLARE `sch 4 fee` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 no fee`
    `sch 4 a fixed sum` HAS `sch 4 the sum` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a sum for each unit, subject to a minimum` HAS `sch 4 the sum for each unit` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the unit` IS A STRING, `sch 4 the minimum` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` HAS `sch 4 the percentage` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the amount it is a percentage of` IS A STRING, `sch 4 the minimum sum` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a fixed sum plus a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` HAS `sch 4 the fixed sum` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the percentage of the amount` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the least sum` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a sum for each document plus a sum for each page` HAS `sch 4 the sum for each document` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the sum for each page` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 the fee for the last application plus a sum` HAS `sch 4 the sum added` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a fee for each page in excess of a limit, rising by steps` HAS `sch 4 the first step and each step` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the highest sum for a page` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a sum for a subscriber and a sum for anyone else` HAS `sch 4 the sum for a subscriber` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the sum for anyone else` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the unit of the sums for a subscriber and anyone else` IS A STRING
    `sch 4 a fee the Registrar finds fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum` HAS `sch 4 the least sum the Registrar may find` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a sum for each day from a day onwards` HAS `sch 4 the sum for each day from the day` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the first day charged` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a sum for each day within a band of days` HAS `sch 4 the sum for each day in the band` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the first day of the band` IS A NUMBER, `sch 4 the last day of the band` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 a fee stated in words` HAS `sch 4 the words of the fee` IS A STRING

-- One row of a table.  `sch 4 row columns` names the column of each fee in `sch 4 row fees`, in the order the text states them;
-- it is empty when the row prints no cell of its own (a heading row, whose fees are in the rows under it).
-- Where the cells of a row do not number the columns of the table (the converter lost the column marks), the generator assigns the columns
-- by what the text says of the row and writes the reason above the row; a cell printed once for two columns appears once for each.
DECLARE `sch 4 row` HAS
    `sch 4 row part`        IS A NUMBER
    `sch 4 row item`        IS A STRING
    `sch 4 row description` IS A STRING
    `sch 4 row columns`     IS A LIST OF `sch 4 column`
    `sch 4 row fees`        IS A LIST OF `sch 4 fee`
    `sch 4 row remarks`     IS A STRING

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Fourth Schedule -- finding the fee in a column`
-- ===========================================================================

GIVEN columns IS A LIST OF `sch 4 column`
      fees IS A LIST OF `sch 4 fee`
      column IS A `sch 4 column`
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 4 fee`
`sch 4 the fee in the column among these` MEANS
    CONSIDER columns
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY crest THEN
        CONSIDER fees
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column
        WHEN f FOLLOWED BY frest THEN
            IF c EQUALS column
            THEN JUST f
            ELSE `sch 4 the fee in the column among these` crest frest column

GIVEN row IS A `sch 4 row`
      column IS A `sch 4 column`
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 4 fee`
`sch 4 the fee in the row for the column` MEANS `sch 4 the fee in the column among these` (row's `sch 4 row columns`) (row's `sch 4 row fees`) column

-- The column the Schedule uses for a claim.  "Supreme Court" has two columns by the value of the claim.
-- The value is Order 25, Rule 2's (seam S-V1); Order 25, Rule 2(2)(d) deems a claim of none of the listed kinds to have a value of up to $1 million.
GIVEN `the court system` IS A `Court system`
      `the court level` IS A `Court level`
      `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 4 column`
`sch 4 the column for the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court system`
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN
        IF `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` AT MOST 1000000
        THEN JUST `sch 4 column Supreme Court up to $1 million`
        ELSE JUST `sch 4 column Supreme Court more than $1 million`
    WHEN `State Courts` THEN
        CONSIDER `the court level`
        WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST `sch 4 column District Court`
        WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST `sch 4 column Magistrate's Court`
        WHEN `General Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the General Division is not a State Court
        WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Appellate Division is not a State Court
        WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Court of Appeal is not a State Court
        WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Singapore International Commercial Court is not a State Court
        WHEN `Family Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Family Division is not a State Court

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Fourth Schedule -- the arithmetic`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The fee for pages in excess of a page limit: "first 10 pages or less exceeding the limit: $a per page; every subsequent 10 pages
-- or less: N + $a per page (where N is the fee payable per page for the previous 10 pages), subject to a maximum of $m per page".
-- The rate of the first ten excess pages is $a; each further ten (or fewer) pages costs $a more per page than the ten before,
-- up to $m per page.
GIVEN pages IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER
      step IS A NUMBER
      `highest rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 4 the fee for pages in excess of a limit, from this step` MEANS
    IF pages AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE (min pages 10) TIMES rate PLUS `sch 4 the fee for pages in excess of a limit, from this step` (pages MINUS 10) (min (rate PLUS step) `highest rate`) step `highest rate`

-- The amount a fee comes to.  `units` is the count the fee is charged on: the pages, days, hours, half days, parties, witnesses, documents,
-- exhibits, attempts, addresses, requests, books, search terms (whichever noun the cell or the row names); it is 1 for a fee of one sum.
-- A fee charged "for each" unit comes to the sum times the count, so a count of 0 owes nothing.
-- A fee charged for the days of a hearing "from" a day, or "within" a band of days, counts the days the hearing lasts: `units` is that number of days.
GIVEN fee IS A `sch 4 fee`
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER fee
    WHEN `sch 4 no fee` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `sch 4 a fixed sum` amount THEN JUST amount
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each unit, subject to a minimum` perUnit unitWords minimum THEN JUST (max (perUnit TIMES units) minimum)
    WHEN `sch 4 a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` percentage ofWords minimum THEN JUST (max (percentage TIMES base DIVIDED BY 100) minimum)
    WHEN `sch 4 a fixed sum plus a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` fixedSum percentage minimum THEN JUST (max (fixedSum PLUS percentage TIMES base DIVIDED BY 100) minimum)
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each document plus a sum for each page` perDocument perPage THEN JUST (perDocument TIMES documents PLUS perPage TIMES units)
    WHEN `sch 4 the fee for the last application plus a sum` added THEN JUST (`the fee payable for the last application` PLUS added)
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee for each page in excess of a limit, rising by steps` step highest THEN JUST (`sch 4 the fee for pages in excess of a limit, from this step` units step step highest)
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each day from a day onwards` perDay firstDay THEN JUST (perDay TIMES (max 0 (units MINUS firstDay PLUS 1)))
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each day within a band of days` perDay firstDay lastDay THEN JUST (perDay TIMES (max 0 ((min units lastDay) MINUS firstDay PLUS 1)))
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for a subscriber and a sum for anyone else` forSubscriber forOther unitWords THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): which of the two sums is charged depends on whether the searcher is a subscriber, which this function is not told; ask `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee for a searcher`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee the Registrar finds fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum` least THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no sum, only that the Registrar finds a fair and reasonable one that is not below the minimum; ask `sch 4 the least sum under the fee`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee stated in words` words THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the cell states the fee in words only and gives no sum to compute

-- The same for a fee that has a subscriber sum and another sum (Part 4 item 1(b)): the searcher's status picks the sum, and the count is the number of
-- search terms (for each module, for each year).  Every other kind of fee comes to what the function above says.
GIVEN fee IS A `sch 4 fee`
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
      `the searcher is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the amount payable under the fee for a searcher` MEANS
    CONSIDER fee
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for a subscriber and a sum for anyone else` forSubscriber forOther unitWords THEN
        JUST (units TIMES (IF `the searcher is a subscriber` THEN forSubscriber ELSE forOther))
    WHEN `sch 4 no fee` THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fixed sum` amount THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each unit, subject to a minimum` perUnit unitWords minimum THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` percentage ofWords minimum THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fixed sum plus a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` fixedSum percentage minimum THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each document plus a sum for each page` perDocument perPage THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 the fee for the last application plus a sum` added THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee for each page in excess of a limit, rising by steps` step highest THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each day from a day onwards` perDay firstDay THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each day within a band of days` perDay firstDay lastDay THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee the Registrar finds fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum` least THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee stated in words` words THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`

-- The least sum a fee can come to when the text leaves the sum to the Registrar and states only a minimum (Part 1 item 43).
-- NOTHING for every other kind of fee: they state a sum, or state nothing.
GIVEN fee IS A `sch 4 fee`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the least sum under the fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER fee
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee the Registrar finds fair and reasonable, subject to a minimum` least THEN JUST least
    WHEN `sch 4 no fee` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a fixed sum` amount THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each unit, subject to a minimum` perUnit unitWords minimum THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` percentage ofWords minimum THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a fixed sum plus a percentage of an amount, subject to a minimum` fixedSum percentage minimum THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each document plus a sum for each page` perDocument perPage THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 the fee for the last application plus a sum` added THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee for each page in excess of a limit, rising by steps` step highest THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each day from a day onwards` perDay firstDay THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for each day within a band of days` perDay firstDay lastDay THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a sum for a subscriber and a sum for anyone else` forSubscriber forOther unitWords THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
    WHEN `sch 4 a fee stated in words` words THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the fee states a sum or no fee, not a minimum
